diff --git a/docs/kamal-deployment.md b/docs/kamal-deployment.md
index 5dcd257..1bfa52f 100644
--- a/docs/kamal-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/kamal-deployment.md
@@ -95,3 +95,19 @@ Optional for S3-compatible endpoints:
 - `S3_REQUEST_CHECKSUM_CALCULATION` (defaults to `when_supported`)
 - `S3_RESPONSE_CHECKSUM_VALIDATION` (defaults to `when_supported`)
 
+
+### Web push notifications
+
+To offer push notifications in notification settings, configure the same stable
+`VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` pair on the web and background-job
+processes. Add both names to `env.secret` in `config/deploy.yml` and their values
+to `.kamal/secrets` (or your secret manager), then redeploy. Only the public key
+is sent to browsers; keep the private key secret. Changing the pair requires
+browsers to subscribe again.
+
+Web push requires HTTPS (localhost is allowed for development). Each person
+opts in separately on each device from **Notification Settings**. On iOS, install
+Fizzy on the Home Screen first. Push delivery runs through the existing job queue;
+expired device subscriptions are removed automatically. `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`
+supplies the contact address used for VAPID. Without both keys, web push stays
+disabled and tray and email notifications continue to work normally.
